<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.craig.estimator.otel — launchd job for scripts/otel-receiver.ts (design §P2.3).

  ############################################################################
  #  NOT INSTALLED. This file is the reviewable source; installing it is a    #
  #  deliberate LAND-TIME step, not something a build does on Craig's         #
  #  behalf. Nothing in Phase 2 depends on it running: with no receiver       #
  #  there is no duration_ms, no reconciliation and no auxiliary spend, the   #
  #  [unvalidated] marker simply stays, and every verb keeps its exit code.   #
  #  Once installed, the copy under ~/Library/LaunchAgents is a SNAPSHOT of   #
  #  this file — editing this one alone changes nothing.                      #
  ############################################################################

  This is a SECOND job, not a modification of com.craig.estimator: that one is a
  03:30 calendar sweep and must stay a calendar job. `launchctl bootstrap`
  refuses a duplicate Label, which is why the label differs.

  Before installing, the settings.json env block (§P2.3) has to exist, or the
  harness exports nothing and this process sits idle on a healthy socket:

      "env": {
        "CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY": "1",
        "OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER": "otlp",
        "OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER": "otlp",
        "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL": "http/json",
        "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT": "http://127.0.0.1:4318",
        "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_METRICS_TEMPORALITY_PREFERENCE": "delta",
        "OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL": "60000",
        "OTEL_LOGS_EXPORT_INTERVAL": "5000",
        "OTEL_METRICS_INCLUDE_SESSION_ID": "true",
        "OTEL_METRICS_INCLUDE_VERSION": "true",
        "OTEL_METRICS_INCLUDE_ACCOUNT_UUID": "false"
      }

  Note the endpoint carries NO path suffix: the generic variable has /v1/logs,
  /v1/metrics and /v1/traces appended by the exporter, so `…:4318/v1/logs` here
  produces requests to `…/v1/logs/v1/logs`, which this receiver answers 404 and
  which looks exactly like a receiver that is not running.

  To install (first time):

      cp ~/.claude/estimator/scripts/com.craig.estimator.otel.plist \
         ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.craig.estimator.otel.plist
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.craig.estimator.otel.plist
      launchctl enable gui/$(id -u)/com.craig.estimator.otel

  To re-install after editing this file (bootstrap refuses an already-loaded
  label, so bootout first — in-flight telemetry is lost, which is one export
  interval of data):

      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.craig.estimator.otel
      cp ~/.claude/estimator/scripts/com.craig.estimator.otel.plist \
         ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.craig.estimator.otel.plist
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.craig.estimator.otel.plist

  To check on it / remove it:

      curl -s http://127.0.0.1:4318/healthz | jq .
      launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.craig.estimator.otel
      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.craig.estimator.otel

  Notes, and each one differs deliberately from the calendar job:
    * RunAtLoad is TRUE — the opposite of the cron job. A receiver that starts at
      the next login loses everything before it.
    * KeepAlive SuccessfulExit=false restarts a CRASH but not a clean shutdown,
      so `launchctl bootout` does not fight a respawn loop.
    * ThrottleInterval 30 stops a port conflict becoming a spin: the receiver
      exits non-zero on a bind failure, deliberately, and without a throttle
      launchd would restart it as fast as it can fail.
    * PATH is set explicitly (launchd inherits no login PATH) and bun is invoked
      by absolute path with a fallback, matching est-lib.sh's probe order.
    * EST_OTEL_MAX_BODY_MB mirrors the `otel_max_body_mb` config row: the
      receiver never opens the database (it must never contend for the writer
      lock), so its one tunable arrives through the environment.
    * Logs go to ~/Library/Logs — outside the dotfiles repo, so nothing here ever
      shows up in `git status`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.craig.estimator.otel</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/sh</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>exec "$(command -v bun || echo /opt/homebrew/bin/bun)" run /Users/craig/.claude/estimator/scripts/otel-receiver.ts</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/Users/craig/.bun/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/craig</string>
        <key>EST_HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/craig/.claude/estimator</string>
        <key>EST_OTEL_PORT</key>
        <string>4318</string>
        <key>EST_OTEL_MAX_BODY_MB</key>
        <string>8</string>
    </dict>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/craig/.claude/estimator</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>

    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>30</integer>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>

    <key>LowPriorityIO</key>
    <true/>

    <key>Nice</key>
    <integer>5</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/craig/Library/Logs/com.craig.estimator.otel.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/craig/Library/Logs/com.craig.estimator.otel.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
